IMPORT prelude

-- A New Tax System (Family Assistance) Act 1999 (Cth) AS IN FORCE ON 30 AUGUST 2006 -- a dated arm beside fa-families.l4
-- (REQ-0062, 22 October 2026): the maternity payment (ss 36, 37, 66; Schedule 4 item 17A), since repealed, and what a second
-- child under 13 added to Family Tax Benefit in 2006 (Schedule 1 cll 2, 3 step 1, 7, 30, 38A).
--
-- SEAT: the parent -- "Am I eligible for the maternity payment for my new baby, and how much is it?", "What does my second
-- child add to my Family Tax Benefit?". Jake's parents, k002 (Jake born 30 August 2006; Chloe born 14 March 2003).
--
-- Edition: register id C2006C00402 (no compilation number), prepared on 1 July 2006 taking into account amendments up to Act
-- No. 82 of 2006, in force from 1 July 2006 to 27 September 2006, as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A00490.2006-07-01.txt (converted from the Register's EPUB; the .DOC rendering is
-- legacy binary). The Register notes that the compilation "is affected by a retrospective amendment" (Act No. 49 of 2012);
-- nothing encoded here was seen to turn on it (NOTES.md). fa-families.l4 (the 2026 compilation) is untouched; the two modules
-- share no names and are not imported together.
--
-- RATES ARE INPUTS, as in fa-families.l4. Schedule 4 cl 2 lists the FTB child rates, the FTB Part A and Part B gross supplement
-- amounts, the higher income free areas, the Part B standard rates and the maternity payment (item 17A, "MAT", subsection
-- 66(1)) as indexed amounts. The FTB amounts are indexed each 1 July (cl 3 table) and the under-13 and 13-15 child rates may
-- also be reset from the pension (cl 7), so the figures printed in this compilation are not the 2006-07 figures, and the
-- indexed ones are in no deposited text (raised as a ledger entry). Every FTB question takes a `Rates in 2006` record;
-- `the rates as printed in C2006C00402` holds the printed figures, as labelled examples. The maternity payment is the one
-- exception: see `the maternity payment amount in force on`.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: who is a parent, an FTB child or eligible for FTB (asked as facts: the 2026 module encodes the 2026 rules, not
-- these); the Secretary's choices under s 37(2), (3) (asked as facts); s 38 (death of the eligible individual); the
-- maternity immunisation allowance (ss 39-41, 67); how and when the payment is made (the Administration Act: s 38 of this Act
-- refers to amounts paid "under subsection 47(2)" of that Act -- raised as a ledger entry); the transitional rule that no
-- maternity payment is payable where maternity allowance was paid for the child (Notes, Table A); the income tests, Method 2,
-- rent assistance, maintenance, large family supplement and multiple birth allowance (a third child or a multiple birth
-- answers `not covered`); sharing (cl 11); cll 9, 10 (the base FTB child rate for a parent on another payment or not seeking
-- maintenance -- taken not to apply). Dates are written YYYYMMDD.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written with the writing-l4-rules skill from the individual's seat with the 2026-10-18 defaults. No
-- pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `A New Tax System (Family Assistance) Act 1999, as in force on 30 August 2006`

§§ `Answers`

DECLARE `Answer in 2006` IS ONE OF
    `dollars` HAS `value` IS A NUMBER
    `not eligible`
    `not covered: the indexed figure for that day is not in the deposited text`
    `not covered: a third FTB child or a multiple birth (large family supplement, multiple birth allowance)`

§§ `ss 36, 37 -- am I eligible for the maternity payment`

-- s 36(1): "An individual is eligible for maternity payment in respect of a child in any of the 4 cases set out in this
-- section." Each case ends with the same limb: the individual "(i) is eligible for family tax benefit in respect of the child
-- at any time within the period of 13 weeks starting on the day of the child's birth; or (ii) would be so eligible except that
-- the individual's rate of family tax benefit, worked out under Division 1 of Part 4, is nil" (for a stillborn child, "would
-- have been eligible ... assuming the child had not been a stillborn child"; for an adoption, from the day the child is
-- entrusted).
DECLARE `How the child came to me` IS ONE OF
    `I am a parent of the child, born alive`               -- s 36(2)
    `the child was entrusted to my care, and I am not a parent` -- s 36(3)
    `the child was stillborn`                              -- s 36(4)
    `the child was entrusted to me for adoption`           -- s 36(5)

DECLARE `My new child` HAS
    `how`                                                   IS A `How the child came to me`
    `born on`                                               IS A NUMBER
    `FTB eligible for the child within 13 weeks, or would be but for a nil rate` IS A BOOLEAN
    `entrusted to me or my partner within 13 weeks of the birth` IS A BOOLEAN
    `likely to stay in that care for at least 13 weeks`     IS A BOOLEAN
    `entrusted by an authorised party, aged under 2`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `if from overseas, under 2 on arriving in Australia`    IS A BOOLEAN
    `another individual would also be eligible`             IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Secretary determined that I am eligible`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `my percentage under a section 37(3) determination`     IS A NUMBER

-- s 36(2): "(a) the individual is a parent of the child; and (b)" the FTB limb. (3): "(a) the individual is not a parent of the
-- child; and (b) the child is entrusted to the care of the individual or the individual's partner within the period of 13 weeks
-- starting on the day of the child's birth; and (c) the child continues, or is likely to continue, in that care for not less
-- than 13 weeks; and (d)" the FTB limb. (4): "(a) the child is a stillborn child; and (b)" the FTB limb, assuming a live
-- birth. (5): "(a) as part of the process for the adoption of the child by the individual, the child is entrusted to the care
-- of the individual by an authorised party; and (b) the child is aged under 2 at the time ...; and (ba) if the child arrives in
-- Australia from overseas as part of the process for the adoption of the child -- the child is aged under 2 when the child
-- arrives in Australia; and (c)" the FTB limb.
GIVEN `c` IS A `My new child`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`one of the four cases in section 36 applies` MEANS
        `c`'s `FTB eligible for the child within 13 weeks, or would be but for a nil rate`
    AND (CONSIDER `c`'s `how`
         WHEN `I am a parent of the child, born alive` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `the child was entrusted to my care, and I am not a parent` THEN
                 `c`'s `entrusted to me or my partner within 13 weeks of the birth`
             AND `c`'s `likely to stay in that care for at least 13 weeks`
         WHEN `the child was stillborn` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `the child was entrusted to me for adoption` THEN
                 `c`'s `entrusted by an authorised party, aged under 2`
             AND `c`'s `if from overseas, under 2 on arriving in Australia`)

-- s 37(1): "Only one individual is eligible for maternity payment in respect of a child." (2): "If 2 or more individuals would
-- otherwise be eligible ..., the individual who is eligible is the one determined by the Secretary to be eligible." (3) the
-- Secretary may instead find it reasonable that 2 or more are eligible, each for a percentage; (4) never both members of a
-- couple. The Secretary's determination is asked as a fact. Both parents in a couple (Graham and Sue, k002) would each
-- otherwise be eligible, so s 37(2) applies: one of them, as the Secretary determines.
@export Am I eligible for the maternity payment for my new child (ss 36, 37)?
GIVEN `c` IS A `My new child` @desc How the child came to you, when, whether you were eligible for Family Tax Benefit for the child within 13 weeks, and whether someone else would also be eligible and what the Secretary determined
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I eligible for the maternity payment` IF
        `one of the four cases in section 36 applies` `c`
    AND (    (NOT `c`'s `another individual would also be eligible`)
          OR `c`'s `the Secretary determined that I am eligible`)

§§ `s 66, Schedule 4 item 17A -- how much`

-- s 66(1): "The amount of maternity payment in respect of a child is $4,000." Schedule 4 cl 2 item 17A lists it as indexed
-- ("Maternity payment | MAT | [subsection 66(1)]"), and the cl 3 table indexes MAT on "(a) 20 March (b) 20 September". The
-- $4,000 took effect on 1 July 2006 (Act No. 59, 2004, s 2(1) item 4: Schedule 2 Part 3 commences on 1 July 2006 unless the
-- indexed amount had by then passed $4,000; the compilation incorporates it). s 3(1) "current figure": an amount not yet
-- indexed "is the amount". From 1 July 2006 to 19 September 2006 no indexation day passed, so the amount in force was the
-- printed $4,000. From 20 September 2006 it is an indexed figure no deposited text holds; before 1 July 2006 it is another
-- compilation's. READING: the amount is the one in force on the day of the birth (for an adoption, on the day the child is
-- entrusted -- the day to give); the Act ties it to "the child", not to a claim or payment date.
@export What was the maternity payment amount in force on a day (s 66(1); Schedule 4 item 17A)?
GIVEN `day` IS A NUMBER @desc The day of the birth (or of the entrustment), YYYYMMDD
GIVETH AN `Answer in 2006`
`the maternity payment amount in force on` MEANS
    IF `day` AT LEAST 20060701 AND `day` LESS THAN 20060920
    THEN `dollars` 4000
    ELSE `not covered: the indexed figure for that day is not in the deposited text`

-- s 66(2): "if, because of determinations by the Secretary under subsection 37(3), 2 or more individuals are eligible ..., each
-- individual is eligible only for the individual's percentage of maternity payment determined under that subsection." The
-- percentage is 100 where there is no s 37(3) determination.
@export How much maternity payment do I get for my new child (ss 36, 37, 66)?
GIVEN `c` IS A `My new child` @desc Your new child, as for the eligibility question; the percentage is 100 unless the Secretary set one under s 37(3)
GIVETH AN `Answer in 2006`
`How much maternity payment do I get` MEANS
    IF NOT `Am I eligible for the maternity payment` `c`
    THEN `not eligible`
    ELSE CONSIDER `the maternity payment amount in force on` (`c`'s `born on`)
         WHEN `dollars` `amount` THEN `dollars` (`amount` TIMES `c`'s `my percentage under a section 37(3) determination` DIVIDED BY 100)
         OTHERWISE `not covered: the indexed figure for that day is not in the deposited text`

§§ `Schedule 1 -- what a second child adds to Family Tax Benefit (2006)`

-- The amounts Schedule 4 indexes, as they stood on the day asked about (inputs). Gloss: the FTB child rate is the yearly
-- amount Part A pays for each child before the income test.
DECLARE `Rates in 2006` HAS
    `FTB under 13 child rate (A1)`                IS A NUMBER  -- Sch 1 cl 7 item 1; Sch 4 item 1
    `FTB gross supplement amount (A)`             IS A NUMBER  -- Sch 1 cl 38A(3); Sch 4 item 8A
    `FTB additional HIFA (A)`                     IS A NUMBER  -- Sch 1 cl 2 column 2; Sch 4 item 12
    `FTB standard rate (B), youngest under 5`     IS A NUMBER  -- Sch 1 cl 30 item 1; Sch 4 item 9
    `FTB standard rate (B), youngest 5 or over`   IS A NUMBER  -- Sch 1 cl 30 item 2; Sch 4 item 9

-- The figures printed in C2006C00402 (Sch 1 cl 7 item 1 "$2,920.00"; cl 38A(3) "$600"; cl 2 column 2 "$3,000"; cl 30 items 1
-- and 2 "$2,569.60" and "$1,781.20"). Labelled examples only: not the 2006-07 figures (see the header).
`the rates as printed in C2006C00402` MEANS `Rates in 2006` WITH
    `FTB under 13 child rate (A1)`              IS 2920
    `FTB gross supplement amount (A)`           IS 600
    `FTB additional HIFA (A)`                   IS 3000
    `FTB standard rate (B), youngest under 5`   IS 2569.60
    `FTB standard rate (B), youngest 5 or over` IS 1781.20

-- Sch 1 cl 3 Step 1: the maximum rate (Method 1) adds "(a) the individual's standard rate ... (b) ... large family supplement
-- (if any) ... (c) ... multiple birth allowance (if any) ... (ca) ... FTB Part A supplement ... (d) ... rent assistance (if
-- any)". cl 7: "The standard rate is the sum of the FTB child rates"; item 1, "FTB child who is under 13 years of age". cl
-- 38A(1)(b): "if the individual has 2 or more FTB children -- the sum of the applicable supplement amounts for each of those
-- children"; (2)(b) the FTB gross supplement amount. cl 34: large family supplement "if the individual has 3 or more FTB
-- children"; cl 36: multiple birth allowance for 3 or more born at once (both `not covered`). So a new FTB child under 13, not
-- shared and not the third, adds its FTB child rate and one FTB gross supplement amount (A). Rent assistance is not encoded.
@export What does a new FTB child under 13 add to my maximum rate of FTB Part A a year (Sch 1 cll 3, 7, 34, 36, 38A, as in 2006)?
GIVEN `the rates` IS A `Rates in 2006` @desc The indexed FTB amounts in force on the day
      `FTB children before the new child` IS A NUMBER @desc How many FTB children you had before the new child
      `born in a multiple birth` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the new child was one of a multiple birth
GIVETH AN `Answer in 2006`
`What a new child under 13 adds to my maximum Part A rate` MEANS
    IF `FTB children before the new child` PLUS 1 AT LEAST 3 OR `born in a multiple birth`
    THEN `not covered: a third FTB child or a multiple birth (large family supplement, multiple birth allowance)`
    ELSE `dollars` (`the rates`'s `FTB under 13 child rate (A1)` PLUS `the rates`'s `FTB gross supplement amount (A)`)

-- Sch 1 cl 2: "An individual's higher income free area is the basic amount in column 1 plus an additional amount in column 2
-- for each FTB child of the individual (after the first)." A second or later child raises it by the additional amount.
@export By how much does a new FTB child raise my higher income free area for FTB Part A (Sch 1 cl 2, as in 2006)?
GIVEN `the rates` IS A `Rates in 2006` @desc The indexed FTB amounts in force on the day
      `FTB children before the new child` IS A NUMBER @desc How many FTB children you had before the new child
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much a new child raises my higher income free area` MEANS
    IF `FTB children before the new child` AT LEAST 1 THEN `the rates`'s `FTB additional HIFA (A)` ELSE 0

-- Sch 1 cl 30: the Part B standard rate is "$2,569.60" where the "youngest FTB child is under 5 years of age" and "$1,781.20"
-- where the "youngest FTB child is 5 years of age or over". A newborn is the youngest and under 5. If the youngest child
-- before was already under 5 (Chloe was 3 in August 2006), the standard rate does not change. cl 31A: one FTB (B) gross
-- supplement amount whatever the number of children.
@export How much does a new child change my FTB Part B standard rate a year (Sch 1 cl 30, as in 2006)?
GIVEN `the rates` IS A `Rates in 2006` @desc The indexed FTB amounts in force on the day
      `FTB children before the new child` IS A NUMBER @desc How many FTB children you had before the new child
      `age of the youngest of them` IS A NUMBER @desc The age in whole years of your youngest FTB child before the new child (any number if none)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much a new child changes my Part B standard rate` MEANS
    IF `FTB children before the new child` LESS THAN 1
    THEN `the rates`'s `FTB standard rate (B), youngest under 5`
    ELSE IF `age of the youngest of them` LESS THAN 5
         THEN 0
         ELSE `the rates`'s `FTB standard rate (B), youngest under 5` MINUS `the rates`'s `FTB standard rate (B), youngest 5 or over`
